<title>TURKEY: Turkish Yapi Kredi signs $150-mln syndicated loan.</title>
<headline>Turkish Yapi Kredi signs $150-mln syndicated loan.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's private  Yapi Kredi Bank signed an accord on Friday for a $150 million syndicated loan from 28 banks, led by the Union Bank of Switzerland, the bank said in a statament.</p>
<p>It said the one-year pre-export financing facility carried an interest of Libor plus 0.5 percent.</p>
<p>The accord was signed in London.</p>
</text>
